27 representations applying to the Company and its restricted subsidiaries:
- existence and power; authorisation and no contravention; approvals; enforceability;
- financial statements and no MAE; no material litigation; no default; property, liens and investments;
- insurance; environmental; taxpayer ID; taxes; ERISA; subsidiaries and Loan Parties;
- use of proceeds and margin stock; Investment Company Act; disclosure; compliance with laws; IP;
- solvency; labour; collateral documents; PATRIOT Act, OFAC and anti-corruption;
- no Affected Financial Institution; foreign obligors; Beneficial Ownership certification; Outbound Investment Rules.

rows.ca_value:
Amendment No. 4 s.2 conditions to the Amendment No. 4 Effective Date:
- executed Amendment; Notes on request; resolution, incumbency and good-standing certificates;
- opinions of Faegre Drinker Biddle & Reath LLP and, for the Dutch Borrower, Baker & McKenzie Amsterdam N.V.;
- officer's certificate; CFO solvency certificate; UCC, tax and judgment lien searches;
- Request for Credit Extension and Funding Indemnity Letter;
- no MAE since December 31, 2025;
- KYC / PATRIOT Act and Beneficial Ownership deliverables (5 Business Days prior);
- payment of fees and expenses; Amendment reps true;
- repayment of all existing loans and termination of existing revolving commitments.
CA s.4.01 cross-refers to these conditions.

rows.ts_value:
Each extension of credit after the Effective Date requires a customary borrowing notice and:
- reps true in all material respects (in all respects if materiality-qualified);
- no event of default or incipient default;
- for multicurrency extensions, no change in national or international financial, political or economic conditions, or in exchange rates or controls, that makes the currency impracticable;
- Designated Borrower requirements satisfied.

rows.ca_value:
s.4.02 applies to all extensions other than the initial Credit Extension and conversions/continuations, and is subject to the LCT provisions in s.1.03(d)(iii). Conditions:
- reps true in all material respects (in all respects if qualified by materiality/MAE);
- no Default;
- Request for Credit Extension received;
- s.2.15 Designated Borrower conditions met;
- Alternative Currency remains an Eligible Currency (the definition covers changes in currency controls and in national or international financial, political or economic conditions).
Each request is a deemed representation.

rows.ts_value:
Customary events of default, with grace periods and materiality thresholds consistent with the Existing Credit Agreement, some applying only to the Company and Significant Subsidiaries:
- non-payment in the required currency;
- covenant breach after specified grace periods;
- misrepresentation;
- cross-default above $75M;
- bankruptcy (with grace period for involuntary proceedings);
- inability to pay debts;
- monetary judgments above $75M and material non-monetary judgments;
- ERISA above $75M;
- invalidity of documents;
- loss of security over a material portion of Collateral;
- change of control.

rows.ca_value:
s.8.01:
- non-payment: principal when due; interest and fees within 3 Business Days; other amounts within 5 Business Days;
- specified covenants immediate; other covenants after 30 days;
- reps incorrect in any material respect;
- cross-payment / cross-acceleration default and swap termination value above the Threshold Amount ($75M), applying to any Loan Party or Restricted Subsidiary;
- insolvency of a Loan Party or Significant Subsidiary (2% test), with a 60-day grace for involuntary proceedings (15 days for frivolous Dutch petitions);
- inability to pay debts / attachment (30 days);
- judgments above $75M to the extent not covered by insurance from an A-rated insurer that has not disputed coverage, or non-monetary MAE judgments (10 Business Day stay window);
- ERISA above $75M;
- invalidity of Loan Documents;
- Change of Control;
- Collateral Documents ceasing to create perfected first-priority Liens on a material amount of Collateral.

rows.ts_value:
Consolidated EBITDA of the Company and restricted subsidiaries includes add-backs for:
- (a) pro forma run-rate cost savings and synergies expected within 18 months;
- (b) non-cash charges, with cash-payment recapture;
- (c) non-controlling interest charges;
- (d) senior officer and management transfers, relocation, hiring and severance;
- (e) integration or startup costs.
Add-backs (a) and (e) share a combined cap of 30% of Consolidated EBITDA (calculated after the add-backs).

CNI excludes (a)-(o):
- extraordinary and non-recurring items; Primex Ltd. income; accounting changes;
- disposal and extinguishment gains/losses; purchase accounting; impairments;
- non-cash compensation; earn-outs; FX;
- unrestricted subsidiary and NCI income;
- transaction costs, including restructuring, closure, reallocation or relocation (including severance);
- (l) liability, casualty and business-interruption losses;
- JV income except cash distributions; pre-acquisition income;
- dividend-restricted non-guarantor income.

rows.ca_value:
CNI exclusions (a)-(p) generally match, but Primex Ltd. income is excluded except for cash actually distributed to the Company or a Restricted Subsidiary. In addition:
- (j) the transaction-cost exclusion omits closure, reallocation, relocation and severance;
- (m) casualty and business-interruption losses are excluded only to the extent covered by insurance and reimbursed (or reasonably evidenced and reimbursed within 365 days);
- (p) the dividend-restricted non-guarantor income exclusion applies only when computing the Cumulative Available Amount builder.

