Affirmative covenants:
- financial statements, budgets and forecasts; certificates; notices;
- payment of obligations and taxes; existence; properties; insurance;
- compliance with laws and material contracts; books and records; inspection; use of proceeds;
- guarantees and security (including on a Collateral Reinstatement Event);
- environmental; approvals; further assurances; anti-corruption;
- Beneficial Ownership Regulation; designation as senior debt.

rows.ca_value:
Article VI, ss.6.01-6.18 (s.6.16 reserved), covers each TS item except compliance with material contracts:
- financial statements and forecasts (s.6.01); certificates and KYC / Beneficial Ownership information (s.6.02(g)); notices, including defaults under Contractual Obligations (s.6.03);
- payment of obligations and material taxes (s.6.04); existence (s.6.05); properties (s.6.06); insurance (s.6.07);
- compliance with Laws only, with no material-contracts limb (s.6.08); books and records (s.6.09); inspection (s.6.10); use of proceeds (s.6.11);
- guarantee and security, including the reinstatement linkage (s.6.12); approvals (s.6.13); environmental (s.6.14); further assurances (s.6.15);
- senior debt designation (s.6.17); anti-corruption (s.6.18).

rows.ts_value:
Restrictions on:
- fundamental changes; prepayments of subordinated debt; sale-leasebacks;
- changes in nature of business; affiliate transactions; burdensome agreements;
- use of proceeds; amendments of organisational documents;
- changes in fiscal year or accounting policies.

rows.ca_value:
s.10.04(a): the Company pays:
- (i) the AA's reasonable out-of-pocket costs of syndication, preparation, negotiation, execution, administration and amendments, with counsel limited to one primary, one special/regulatory and one local counsel per jurisdiction;
- (ii) L/C Issuer expenses;
- (iii) enforcement and workout expenses of the AA, Arrangers, Lenders and L/C Issuer, with the counsel caps plus conflicts counsel.
Amounts are payable within 10 Business Days of demand.
